# Paths whose diff needs human eyes, regardless of what the measurement says.
#
# This file mirrors the eval scorer's taint set (scripts/eval_scorer.py:
# INFRA_FILES, INFRA_PREFIXES, SUPPLY_CHAIN_FILES, SUPPLY_CHAIN_PREFIXES,
# PINNED_DIRS). Both express the same policy — "the pipeline cannot vouch for
# this on its own" — so they are kept in sync by a test
# (tests/eval/test_pr_eval_bot.py, CodeownersMirrorsTaint). Add a path to the
# taint set and this file must grow an entry too, or that test fails.
#
# Why both, when the taint set already caps such a PR at eval:tainted:
#
#   * The taint cap only exists if an eval RAN. A PR touching only cmake/ or
#     Dockerfile is not a runtime path, so no eval is triggered, no eval:*
#     label is applied, and the taint policy never gets a say.
#   * The bot can be down. It has been: a bad gh field killed every poll, and
#     a rented spot GPU can be unavailable for hours. A guard that depends on
#     the bot running is not a guard against the bot being broken.
#
# CODEOWNERS is enforced by GitHub itself and holds in both cases.
#
# NOTE: on its own this file only REQUESTS review. It blocks nothing until
# branch protection on main sets required_pull_request_reviews with
# require_code_owner_reviews = true. See CONTRIBUTING.md.

# --- eval infrastructure: the bot, the policy it applies, how it is run -----
/scripts/pr_eval_bot.py         @dripsmvcp
/scripts/eval_scorer.py         @dripsmvcp
/scripts/pr_eval_cron.sh        @dripsmvcp
/scripts/provision_eval_box.sh  @dripsmvcp
# The offline verifier. Not in the scorer's taint set (it runs on a reader's
# machine, never in the eval), but a weakened verifier makes a published
# receipt say more than it proves.
/scripts/verify_receipt.py      @dripsmvcp

# --- CI, the merge gate, and this file itself -------------------------------
/.github/                       @dripsmvcp

# --- the pinned harness: what the verdict is measured BY --------------------
/bench/                         @dripsmvcp
/tests/                         @dripsmvcp

# --- supply chain: what the build pulls in, how the container starts --------
/cmake/                         @dripsmvcp
/Dockerfile                     @dripsmvcp
/docker-entrypoint.sh           @dripsmvcp
/docker-compose.yml             @dripsmvcp
